# Build bundles for external typesetting (Overleaf and the like). These are
# DERIVED from paper/*.tex and paper/references.bib, which are already
# versioned, so committing one stores a second copy of the paper that goes stale
# the moment any section changes.
#
# It is also a linter blind spot. check_paper.py's SCAN_EXTS covers .tex and
# .md, never .zip, so a withdrawn number sealed inside an archive rides past a
# green STALE_CLAIM invisibly. The one thing worse than a stale claim is a stale
# claim no gate can see.
#
# And it is how the current push blocker was created: docs/audit_sources_*.tar.gz
# entered at cc357db, every commit since carries the blob, and bb45528 sits in
# that range and is cited in the signed, frozen Amendment 2. Removing it now
# needs a history rewrite that would invalidate a signature's provenance chain.
# Regenerate the bundle instead; it takes seconds.
docs/*.zip
